; Carry-over. Each month starts with what was available at the end of the previous one, months without any entry
; included; an overspent budget carries its negative amount over; a budget-add may be negative, and a transfer may
; leave a budget below zero. `added` is what the month's directives put in, `assigned` adds the carry-over.
option "operating_currency" "CNY"
option "timezone" "UTC"

1970-01-01 commodity CNY

2024-01-01 open Assets:Bank
2024-01-01 open Expenses:Rent
  budget: Rent
2024-01-01 open Expenses:Food
  budget: Food

2024-01-01 budget Rent CNY
2024-01-01 budget Food CNY
2024-01-01 budget-add Rent 3000 CNY
2024-01-01 budget-add Food 500 CNY

2024-01-03 * "Landlord" "January rent"
  Expenses:Rent 2800 CNY
  Assets:Bank

2024-01-20 * "Market" "overspending"
  Expenses:Food 650 CNY
  Assets:Bank

; February: nothing at all

; March: Food gets money from Rent, and Rent overspends
2024-03-01 budget-add Food 400 CNY
2024-03-02 budget-transfer Rent Food 300 CNY

2024-03-03 * "Landlord" "March rent"
  Expenses:Rent 2900 CNY
  Assets:Bank

2024-03-15 budget-add Rent -100 CNY

; May: a refund
2024-05-10 * "Market" "a refund"
  Expenses:Food -30 CNY
  Assets:Bank
